Fixed. The bug was in the URL comparison at `src/import_merge.ts:7`.

**Root cause:** `result.find((b) => b.url === inc.url)` did a raw string comparison, so `https://example.com/a` ≠ `https://EXAMPLE.com/a` — different hostname casing wasn't recognized as a duplicate.

**Fix:** Normalize each URL's hostname to lowercase before comparing (paths remain case-sensitive, since only the hostname is case-insensitive per the URL spec). Falls back to a raw string compare for URLs that fail to parse.

Verified with a test: the case-differing URL now merges into the existing entry (tags unioned to `x,y`, single entry), while a genuinely different URL still appends.


